%% §21 machine 5 of 8 — Deliverable  (Prisma enum: DeliverableState)
%% §21: NOT_STARTED -> DRAFT_SUBMITTED -> BTG_REVIEW -> SPONSOR_REVIEW -> APPROVED -> PUBLISHED -> VERIFIED
    direction TB
    [*] --> NOT_STARTED : created with the order
    NOT_STARTED --> DRAFT_SUBMITTED : athlete uploads a draft
    DRAFT_SUBMITTED --> BTG_REVIEW : content approval queue
    BTG_REVIEW --> SPONSOR_REVIEW : BTG passes it on
    BTG_REVIEW --> DRAFT_SUBMITTED : changes requested (derived)
    SPONSOR_REVIEW --> APPROVED : sponsor signs off
    SPONSOR_REVIEW --> DRAFT_SUBMITTED : changes requested (derived)
    APPROVED --> PUBLISHED : athlete posts it, publishedUrl captured
    PUBLISHED --> VERIFIED : BTG confirms the live post
    VERIFIED --> [*]

    note right of BTG_REVIEW
      §21 states the forward path only. Both review
      states need a way back or a rejected draft has
      nowhere to go; the two return arrows are derived
      and confirmed in P2-BE-02.
    end note
    note right of VERIFIED
      VERIFIED is a measured fact, not a claim:
      metrics recorded against this deliverable carry
      their own MetricSource provenance.
    end note
